The flashbang animation of the Light switch
-------------------------------------------
The animation that plays when the mixer page turns light (the grenade that
rolls in, the white flash and the fade) is the work of Silvertree2010, taken
from ApolloOffice:

    https://github.com/Silvertree2010/ApolloOffice  (ui/th.js and three rules
    of ui/index.html, release 0.10.4)

    Written by Silvertree2010
    Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3

It sits in gui/gui.html, between the lines "---- the flashbang" and
"function applyTheme", and in the style block with the id "flashbang-css".
The timings, the movement and the pixel grenade are his, unchanged. What we
changed: the code is a function of this page (it switches the page's theme
instead of his data-th), the grenade has a longer constant name, and a
second call while one is playing switches at once instead of starting a
second flash.

That part stays under the AGPL-3.0 (LICENSE-AGPL-3.0), which the GPL-3.0
allows to be combined with (section 13 of both licences); the rest of
BananaSplit stays GPL-3.0-or-later. BananaSplit is free software and offers
its source to everyone who uses it, which is what the AGPL asks of a program
that people use over a network (here: the mixer page on your own computer).
